      "id": "xhqteilfGucKMGkU",
      "name": "Shielded Recovery",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "xhqteilfGucKMGkU",
        "folder": "QHbygiXRUCPWkCjh",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Shielded Recovery",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You can bandage wounds with the same hand you use to hold your shield. You can use the same hand you are using to wield a shield to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Treat Wounds] or use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Battle Medicine], and you are considered to have a hand free for other uses of Medicine as long as the only thing you are holding or wielding in that hand is a shield. When you use Battle Medicine on an ally while wielding a shield, they gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and Reflex saves that lasts until the start of your next turn or until they are no longer adjacent to you, whichever comes first.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Shielded Recovery]</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Officer's Medical Training"
              }
            ]
          },
